</div></div><div data-layout="Layout2ColumnPadded" class="f fdc lg:fdr lg:sx56 mx20 sm:mx32 xl:mxa xl:mw1200px mb20"><div class="mnw0 sm:px40 lg:px56 x100"><div class="package"><article class="rel"><figure class="rel f m0 fdc -mx20 sm:-mx40 lg:-mx56 x100vw sm:cw-80 lg:cw-112 mb32"><div class="rel x100 block"><picture><source type="image/webp" media="(min-width: 1154px)" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118019/5/ratio3x2_960.webp"/><source type="image/webp" media="(min-width: 1074px)" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118019/5/ratio3x2_720.webp"/><source type="image/webp" media="(min-width: 1048px)" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118019/5/ratio3x2_640.webp"/><source type="image/webp" media="(min-width: 1024px)" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118019/5/ratio3x2_1080.webp"/><source type="image/webp" media="(min-width: 784px)" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118019/5/ratio3x2_960.webp"/><source type="image/webp" media="(min-width: 768px)" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118019/5/ratio3x2_720.webp"/><source type="image/webp" media="(min-width: 768px)" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118019/5/ratio3x2_960.webp"/><source type="image/webp" media="(min-width: 720px)" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118019/5/ratio3x2_768.webp"/><source type="image/webp" media="(min-width: 640px)" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118019/5/ratio3x2_720.webp"/><source type="image/webp" media="(min-width: 480px)" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118019/5/ratio3x2_640.webp"/><source type="image/webp" media="(min-width: 360px)" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118019/5/ratio3x2_480.webp"/><source type="image/webp" media="(min-width: 240px)" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118019/5/ratio3x2_360.webp"/><source type="image/webp" media="(max-width: 239px)" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118019/5/ratio3x2_240.webp"/><img alt="Flavorful, easy to transport and tasty the day after, this abundant summer salad is perfect for summer gatherings." loading="eager" fetchPriority="high" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118019/5/ratio3x2_80.jpg 80w, https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118019/5/ratio3x2_160.jpg 160w, https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118019/5/ratio3x2_240.jpg 240w, https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118019/5/ratio3x2_360.jpg 360w, https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118019/5/ratio3x2_480.jpg 480w, https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118019/5/ratio3x2_640.jpg 640w, https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118019/5/ratio3x2_720.jpg 720w, https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118019/5/ratio3x2_960.jpg 960w, https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118019/5/ratio3x2_1080.jpg 1080w, https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118019/5/ratio3x2_1440.jpg 1440w, https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118019/5/ratio3x2_1920.jpg 1920w" sizes="" style="aspect-ratio:3 / 2" class="x100 y100 opc bgpc ofcv bgscv block bg-gray200 mnh0px fill"/></picture></div><figcaption id="mediaCaptionAria" class="f fdc g2 rel pt8 px20 sm:px0 rel"><span class="photoCaption c-gray700 block ya"><div data-server-side-rendered="true" class="r12zgbl0 ruduv2y"><p>Flavorful, easy to transport and tasty the day after, this abundant summer salad is perfect for summer gatherings.</p></div></span><span class="photoCredit c-gray600 block rel z1 mt2 mr48"><span>Amisha Gurbani </span></span></figcaption></figure><div class="pb20"><div id="everlit-auto-audio-widget" data-eid="item-102852" data-publication-id="pblc_kYW067sbmBR" style="height:130px" class="x100 tac fs16"></div></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>Shades of green, red, orange, yellow, purple, magenta, pink greet you at the farmers market this time of year. Each stall brims with a bountiful rainbow of produce, offering an endless array of colors and textures and flavors — crisp, tender, juicy, sweet and earthy. This is California summer at its peak: colorful, abundant and endlessly inspiring.</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>Inspired by all that color and texture, this zucchini, corn and peach orzo salad is a keeper, one that will be on repeat by anyone who makes it. </p></div><div></div><div></div><div></div><div></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>Produce-rich meals have always been a part of my dinner table, and that appreciation for fruits and vegetables has naturally been passed down to my children. Growing up surrounded by a variety of seasonal produce has made them open-minded eaters, eager to try new ingredients and flavors. Their enthusiasm inspires me in the kitchen, encouraging me to create dishes that celebrate fresh produce in delicious ways.</p></div><div class="pt16 sy16 bb bt b-gray300 mb32"><div class=""><p class="uiHeader11 f aic jcc ttu">Advertisement</p><p class="uiTextSmall f aic jcc">Article continues below this ad</p></div><div data-block-type="ad" data-small-id="A300" data-large-id="CONCERT1" data-unit="hnp-sfchronicle.com/article_dtc" class="f jcc mnh250px sm:mnh600px ais lg:f lg:jcc lg:mnh300px lg:ais"></div></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>There is something about the combination of zucchini, sweet corn and juicy peaches that just works miraculously well. Another dish that my family demands every summer, for instance, is my cheese toast featuring them, along with some spicy green chiles and cilantro, on sourdough.</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>My orzo salad starts off with the most delicious basil vinaigrette. Made in a high speed blender, it can be stored in the fridge for up to 2 weeks — if it lasts that long. Next comes the Parmesan-baked zucchini, where zucchini is tossed in olive oil, salt and pepper, and baked in the oven after a generous sprinkle of Parmesan on each side. Flip them halfway through, another sprinkle of Parmesan and bake them to golden perfection. </p></div><div class="mb32"><div class="x100 bg-white f fdc aic mxa p20 deep br4"><div class="f fdc aic mb10"><div class="f aic jcc"><div class="f aic"><div id="badge-logo"><svg width="50" height="50" viewBox="0 0 101 100" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="y100 bubi3gv" role="img" aria-label="San Francisco Chronicle Logo"><desc>San Francisco Chronicle Logo</desc><use href="#logosource-sfchronicle-badge"></use></svg></div></div><div class="pl10 pr10"><svg width="16" height="16" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 13" class="p0"><path id="Path 5" d="M2.50195 2.00183L11.4983 10.9981" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.25" stroke-linecap="round"></path><path id="Path 5_2" d="M2.50195 10.9982L11.4983 2.00187" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.25" stroke-linecap="round"></path></svg></div><svg width="40" height="40" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="p0"><path d="M23.7449 12.27C23.7449 11.48 23.6749 10.73 23.5549 10H12.2549V14.51H18.7249C18.4349 15.99 17.5849 17.24 16.3249 18.09V21.09H20.1849C22.4449 19 23.7449 15.92 23.7449 12.27Z" fill="#4285F4"></path><path d="M12.2549 24C15.4949 24 18.2049 22.92 20.1849 21.09L16.3249 18.09C15.2449 18.81 13.8749 19.25 12.2549 19.25C9.12492 19.25 6.47492 17.14 5.52492 14.29H1.54492V17.38C3.51492 21.3 7.56492 24 12.2549 24Z" fill="#34A853"></path><path d="M5.52488 14.29C5.27488 13.57 5.14488 12.8 5.14488 12C5.14488 11.2 5.28488 10.43 5.52488 9.71V6.62H1.54488C0.724882 8.24 0.254883 10.06 0.254883 12C0.254883 13.94 0.724882 15.76 1.54488 17.38L5.52488 14.29Z" fill="#FBBC05"></path><path d="M12.2549 4.75C14.0249 4.75 15.6049 5.36 16.8549 6.55L20.2749 3.13C18.2049 1.19 15.4949 0 12.2549 0C7.56492 0 3.51492 2.7 1.54492 6.62L5.52492 9.71C6.47492 6.86 9.12492 4.75 12.2549 4.75Z" fill="#EA4335"></path></svg></div></div><h3 class="uiHeader8 tac fs18 mb12 sm:fs23 sm:uiHeader4"><div data-block-type="text" data-server-side-rendered="true" class="r12zgbl0 ruduv2y">See more S.F. Chronicle on Google</div></h3><div data-block-type="text" data-server-side-rendered="true" class="r12zgbl0 ruduv2y uiTextMedium tac c-gray700 mb16">Make us a Preferred Source to get more of our news when you search.</div><a href="https://www.google.com/preferences/source?q=sfchronicle.com" data-link="native" role="button" aria-label="Add Preferred Source" class="td300 cp f aic jcc disabled:cd wsn px24 y40px px16 py8 buttonSm fs13 xs:fs16 xs:buttonLg bg-primaryAccessible hover:o80 c-white disabled:bg-gray300 disabled:c-gray600 border bn tac br2"><div data-block-type="text" data-server-side-rendered="true" class="r12zgbl0 ruduv2y">Add Preferred Source</div></a></div></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>Orzo is an Italian pasta that looks like a long grain of rice or barley and is made with durum wheat semolina or flour. Cook it per the package instructions and cook the corn over a grill or a gas stovetop. If you do not have either, you can strip the corn off the cob, sauté it in a pan with a little bit of butter for a few minutes until golden brown. </p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>The peach is cut simply, into small cubes. Feel free to substitute a white peach or nectarine as well. I love the pop of color from the crimson peel. The salad also has halloumi, a semi-hard, briny cheese from Cyprus that has a high melting point, allowing it to be grilled or pan seared, which gives the outside a chewy texture with soft interiors. </p></div><div class="pt16 sy16 bb bt b-gray300 mb32"><div class=""><p class="uiHeader11 f aic jcc ttu">Advertisement</p><p class="uiTextSmall f aic jcc">Article continues below this ad</p></div><div data-block-type="ad" data-small-id="CONCERT1" data-large-id="CONCERT2" data-unit="hnp-sfchronicle.com/article_dtc" class="f jcc mnh250px sm:mnh300px ais lg:f lg:jcc lg:mnh300px lg:ais"></div></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>All of the ingredients, along with finely chopped oregano and coarsely chopped pistachios, are tossed together with the basil vinaigrette. The salad is garnished with basil leaves and some more pistachios for good measure. </p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>The best part about this orzo salad is how easy it is to transport for a summer get-together. It is best enjoyed with a light wine such as a Riesling.</p></div><figure class="rel f m0 fdc -mx20 sm:mx0 x100vw sm:x100 psup5fr mb32"><div class="rel x100 block"><picture><source type="image/webp" media="(min-width: 1260px)" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118018/5/ratio2x3_960.webp"/><source type="image/webp" media="(min-width: 1186px)" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118018/5/ratio2x3_720.webp"/><source type="image/webp" media="(min-width: 1048px)" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118018/5/ratio2x3_640.webp"/><source type="image/webp" media="(min-width: 874px)" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118018/5/ratio2x3_960.webp"/><source type="image/webp" media="(min-width: 798px)" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118018/5/ratio2x3_720.webp"/><source type="image/webp" media="(min-width: 768px)" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118018/5/ratio2x3_640.webp"/><source type="image/webp" media="(min-width: 768px)" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118018/5/ratio2x3_960.webp"/><source type="image/webp" media="(min-width: 720px)" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118018/5/ratio2x3_768.webp"/><source type="image/webp" media="(min-width: 640px)" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118018/5/ratio2x3_720.webp"/><source type="image/webp" media="(min-width: 480px)" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118018/5/ratio2x3_640.webp"/><source type="image/webp" media="(min-width: 360px)" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118018/5/ratio2x3_480.webp"/><source type="image/webp" media="(min-width: 240px)" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118018/5/ratio2x3_360.webp"/><source type="image/webp" media="(max-width: 239px)" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118018/5/ratio2x3_240.webp"/><img alt="Garnishing the orzo salad with crunchy pistachios, peach slices and basil leaves ensures each bite has a bit of crunch and sweetness. " loading="lazy" srcSet="https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118018/5/ratio2x3_80.jpg 80w, https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118018/5/ratio2x3_160.jpg 160w, https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118018/5/ratio2x3_240.jpg 240w, https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118018/5/ratio2x3_360.jpg 360w, https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118018/5/ratio2x3_480.jpg 480w, https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118018/5/ratio2x3_640.jpg 640w, https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118018/5/ratio2x3_720.jpg 720w, https://s.hdnux.com/photos/01/66/55/13/31118018/5/ratio2x3_960.jpg 960w" sizes="(min-width: 1260px) 960px, (min-width: 1048px) 67vw, (min-width: 768px) 90vw, 100vw" style="aspect-ratio:2 / 3" class="x100 y100 opc bgpc ofcv bgscv block bg-gray200 mnh0px fill"/></picture></div><figcaption id="mediaCaptionAria" class="f fdc g2 rel pt8 px20 sm:px0 rel"><span class="photoCaption c-gray700 block ya"><div data-server-side-rendered="true" class="r12zgbl0 ruduv2y"><p>Garnishing the orzo salad with crunchy pistachios, peach slices and basil leaves ensures each bite has a bit of crunch and sweetness. </p></div></span><span class="photoCredit c-gray600 block rel z1 mt2 mr48"><span>Amisha Gurbani </span></span></figcaption></figure><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p><strong>Zucchini, Corn and Peach Orzo Salad</strong></p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p><em>Serves 6 to 8</em></p></div><div class="pt16 sy16 bb bt b-gray300 mb32"><div class=""><p class="uiHeader11 f aic jcc ttu">Advertisement</p><p class="uiTextSmall f aic jcc">Article continues below this ad</p></div><div data-block-type="ad" data-small-id="B300" data-unit="hnp-sfchronicle.com/article_dtc" class="f jcc mnh250px sm:mnh600px ais lg:none"></div></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>With summer produce at its peak, make this absolutely delightful and fresh salad, with oven-baked Parmesan zucchini, grilled corn, sweet and juicy peaches and grilled halloumi. An herbaceous basil vinaigrette ties it all together. This salad will be perfect for your summer soiree. </p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p><strong>Basil vinaigrette</strong></p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>1 cup fresh basil, tightly packed</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>3 tablespoons lemon juice</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>2 tablespoons sherry or champagne vinegar</p></div><div class="pt16 sy16 bb bt b-gray300 mb32"><div class=""><p class="uiHeader11 f aic jcc ttu">Advertisement</p><p class="uiTextSmall f aic jcc">Article continues below this ad</p></div><div data-block-type="ad" data-small-id="CONCERT2" data-unit="hnp-sfchronicle.com/article_dtc" class="f jcc mnh250px sm:mnh300px ais lg:none"></div></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>2 garlic cloves</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>1 teaspoon black pepper</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>¾ teaspoon salt</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>1 tablespoon honey</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>½ cup extra-virgin olive oil</p></div><div class="pt16 sy16 bb bt b-gray300 mb32"><div class=""><p class="uiHeader11 f aic jcc ttu">Advertisement</p><p class="uiTextSmall f aic jcc">Article continues below this ad</p></div><div data-block-type="ad" data-small-id="S300" data-unit="hnp-sfchronicle.com/article_dtc" class="f jcc mnh250px sm:mnh600px ais lg:none"></div></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p><strong>Parmesan-baked zucchini</strong></p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>1 large or 2 medium-sized zucchini, sliced vertically into half, then sliced into ¼-inch slices</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>2 tablespoons olive oil</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>½ teaspoon salt</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>½ teaspoon black pepper</p></div><div><div data-block-type="ad" data-unit="hnp-sfchronicle.com/article_dtc" class="lg:none"></div></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>½ teaspoon garlic powder</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>⅓ cup grated Parmesan </p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p><strong>Orzo salad</strong></p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>8 ounces halloumi, cut into ⅓-inch slices</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>2 cups orzo, cooked per packaged instructions</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>1 corn on the cob, grilled</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>2 yellow peaches, cut into small cubes</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>2 tablespoons oregano, finely chopped</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>⅓ cup pistachios, coarsely chopped</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p><strong>Garnish</strong></p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>Basil leaves</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>Yellow peach slices</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p><strong>Make the basil vinaigrette:</strong> Add all the ingredients in a high-speed blender and blend to a smooth vinaigrette. Pour it into a glass jar and refrigerate until ready to use.</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p><strong>Make the Parmesan-baked zucchini:</strong> Preheat the oven to 400 degrees. Spray a half baking sheet with cooking spray. Add the sliced zucchini, olive oil, salt, pepper and garlic powder and toss until well combined. Lay them flat such that they are not overlapping. Sprinkle half of the Parmesan onto each zucchini slice. Bake for about 20 to 25 minutes or until the zucchini is golden brown in color. </p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>Using a small offset spatula, flip them over and sprinkle the Parmesan on the slices. Bake for another 20 to 25 minutes or until the zucchini is golden brown in color. Cool completely as it will turn crisp.</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p><strong>Grill the halloumi:</strong> Spray cooking spray on a grill pan on medium heat. Add the halloumi slices, not overlapping each other, and grill for about 2-3 minutes, or until you see golden brown grill marks. Flip and repeat on the other side to get the grill marks. Set aside until ready to toss in the salad.</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p><strong>Combine the ingredients:</strong> In a large platter, add the freshly cooked orzo, while still warm; grilled corn; peaches; grilled halloumi; and oregano. Mix in most of the pistachios, setting about 2 tablespoons aside. Pour the basil vinaigrette all over the orzo salad and toss until well combined.</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p>Garnish with the chopped pistachios, basil leaves and yellow peach slices. Serve at room temperature.</p></div><div class="r1udwkp5 d1uy5mhj articleBody mb32" data-block-type="text" data-dropcap="false"><p><strong>Note:</strong> This dish can be made a day ahead and served at room temperature the next day.</p></div><div></div><div class="y1px x100 abs bgn top"></div><div style="top:25%" class="y1px x100 abs bgn"></div><div style="top:50%" class="y1px x100 abs bgn"></div><div style="top:75%" class="y1px x100 abs bgn"></div><div class="y1px x100 abs bgn bottom"></div></article></div><div class="package"><span class="mb16 blo